@* Blazor's event handlers and two-way binding are directive attributes contributed by tag helpers in
   Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web, and a tag helper only applies where its namespace is in scope.
   Without this file the Razor compiler does not recognize @onclick, @bind, @oninput, @onchange or
   @onkeydown and emits each one as a literal HTML attribute, silently -- nothing in the build says so.

   Nineteen components here carry such an attribute. Before this file existed, eighteen of them had
   every one of theirs dead: 69 handlers and 6 @onclick:stopPropagation / :preventDefault modifiers.
   DashboardLayout was the exception, having imported this namespace itself, so its theme and time zone
   pickers were the only controls in the dashboard that worked. ConfirmDialog was among the eighteen,
   so every action that asks first -- delete a job, unschedule a trigger, shut a scheduler down -- was
   unreachable even where the button that opens the dialog was live. *@
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Forms
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Routing
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web
@using Microsoft.JSInterop
